{"nodes": [{"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_live_integration_suites", "label": "Broker Live-Integration Suites", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Same pattern as the #313 cluster integration setup, one container per suite instead of a 5-node mesh: every adapter is exercised against a live socket rather than a fake."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_hand_rolled_broker_fakes", "label": "Hand-Rolled Broker Fakes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The unit suites test adapters against fakes for fast feedback, which is the right shape but leaves protocol corners, auth bring-up and broker defaults uncovered."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_protocol_level_corners", "label": "Protocol-Level Corners", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Quoting, escaping and header serialisation can differ between our spec-reading and what the real broker accepts."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_auth_connection_bring_up", "label": "Auth and Connection Bring-Up", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Credentials format, TLS and lazy reconnect after a transient drop are invisible to a fake."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_operational_shape", "label": "Operational Shape Defaults", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Broker configuration the code assumed exists but which is not on by default, e.g. Mosquitto's allow_anonymous or RabbitMQ's definitions.json import."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_test_package_manifest", "label": "Dedicated Broker Test Manifest", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A fresh manifest with no peer-dep cross-reference declares every adapter peer-dep plus actor-ts's own runtime deps as plain dependencies, reproducing exactly what an end user's project looks like and side-stepping two bun traps that fire only inside this repo."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_bun_install_production_trap", "label": "bun install --production Peer-Dep Trap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`bun install --production` skips optional peer-deps entirely, so the runner image would ship without the adapter it is meant to test."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_bun_add_optional_peer_trap", "label": "bun add Optional Peer-Dep No-Op Trap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "`bun add <pkg>` silently no-ops when the package is already listed in peerDependencies with optional: true, because bun treats it as already declared."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_waitforport", "label": "waitForPort Readiness Probe", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TCP/HTTP probe used by every scenario to guard the container-started-but-broker-not-ready race, the single most common source of flake."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_scenario_runner", "label": "Broker Scenario Runner", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_runscenarios", "label": "runScenarios", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_suite_directory_shape", "label": "Uniform Suite Directory Shape", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every suite is a docker-compose.<broker>.yml, a Runner.ts importing its scenarios, and a scenarios/ directory, so adding a broker is a copy-and-swap rather than a design exercise."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_testcontainers_rejection", "label": "Rejection of testcontainers/node", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bun compatibility is best-effort (the library expects Node's child_process event ordering), the requirement was locally runnable like tests/integration, and the compose files are ~20 lines each so the abstraction cost outweighs the boilerplate saved."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_per_suite_container_lifecycle", "label": "Per-Suite Container Lifecycle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One broker per suite rather than a fresh broker per it() \u2014 revisitable if per-test lifecycle is ever wanted, but adequate for the current scenario count."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_integration_brokers_ci_matrix", "label": "integration-brokers.yml CI Matrix", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs the broker suites as a job matrix, skipped on PRs touching only docs or unit tests using the same paths: filter as integration.yml."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_tini_pid1_image_preference", "label": "tini-Style PID 1 Image Preference", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Images with a tini-style PID 1 exit cleanly on `docker compose down` instead of leaking zombies."}, {"id": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_readiness_race", "label": "Container-Started Broker-Not-Ready Race", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Named as the single most common source of flake in the broker suites."}], "edges": [{"source": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_hand_rolled_broker_fakes", "target": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_broker_live_integration_suites", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "tests/integration/brokers/README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_hand_rolled_broker_fakes", "target": "tests_integration_brokers_readme_protocol_level_corners", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "c